      "text": [
        " اَلظَّهْرِ يَرْعَى وَ هُوَ يَرْضَى أَنْ يَعْتَمِرَ ثُمَّ يَخْرُجَ فَقَالَ «إِنْ كَانَ اِعْتَمَرَ فِي ذِي اَلْقَعْدَةِ فَحَسَنٌ وَ إِنْ كَانَ فِي ذِي اَلْحِجَّةِ فَلاَ يَصْلُحُ إِلاَّ اَلْحَجُّ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2942 - Abdullah ibn Sinan asked Imam (as) about a servant who is out grazing animals and agrees to perform Umrah and then leave.\nImam (as) said: \"If he performed Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah, it is good. But if it is in Dhu al-Hijjah, then it is not suitable except for Hajj.\""
        ]
      }
